{ 6th move Be2 leading into Scheveningen/classical setup. If white starts with Be2 then black plays Nf6, and if Be3 black is obliged to play a6. After Be2 Nf6 short castle Be7 f4 d6 Kh1 short castle. }
7... Nf6 8. O-O Be7 9. f4 d6 10. Kh1
{ White has two main ideas in Scheveningen: Qe1 Qg3 Kh1 and then play as recommended, or go a4. Kh1 keeps flexibility. }
