12... Nxd4
{ Black plays Nd4 - quite rare but effective. After Qxd4 e5 Qd2 exf4. } 13.
Qxd4 e5 14. Qd2 exf4
{ In all these structures: Be6 Nd7 and Ne5. Once you get Ne5, you don't need help figuring it out - Nc4 Bf6 Be5 and so on. }
15. Bxf4 Be6 16. Rfd1
{ White can also try Ra1d1. The point of Rfd1 or Red1 is to stop Nd7-Ne5. White forces black to place rook on d8, and after Nd7 white can take on e5. }
